      <title>Richard Posner Transformed American Law With Economic Thinking</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-13/richard-posner-transformed-american-law-with-economic-thinking</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">02f12e8a51ef99a50e84752c</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:30:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Judge Richard Posner, who died this week at 87, was the godfather of what is known as the law and economics movement. In a career spanning half a century and some 50 books, 500 articles, and thousands of judicial opinions, he pursued a single organizing idea: The purpose of law, rightly understood, is not to do justice but to pursue economic efficiency.</description>
