      <title>Why Won’t Congress Unlock Cheaper Electricity?</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-13/why-won-t-congress-unlock-cheaper-electricity</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">da7cc1ddb5e3ec80ef90ffe5</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:30:03 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The giant infrastructure permitting bill currently hanging in the balance of a lame duck Congress covers a lot of ground, from pipelines to power grids. One of its unifying objectives is affordability — it’s right there in the title: the Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act, or BAAJA. Cutting red tape for new energy pathways can both reduce their cost and open up sources of cheaper supply to alleviate the growing burden of electricity bills.</description>
      <dc:creator>Liam Denning</dc:creator>
